title: 'Add runtime metadata detection for Aura authority ID'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    This PR adds optional runtime metadata-based detection for Aura authority ID types in `polkadot-omni-node-lib`.
    
    The runtime now scans metadata to determine whether the Aura pallet uses `sr25519` or `ed25519`, falling back to chain spec ID heuristics only when metadata detection unavailable or fails.

    ## Changes Made

    **File: `cumulus/polkadot-omni-node/lib/src/common/runtime.rs`**

    1. **Added `aura_consensus_id()` method to `MetadataInspector`**:
       - Scans runtime metadata types for `sp_consensus_aura::sr25519::AuthorityId` or `sp_consensus_aura::ed25519::AuthorityId` patterns
       - Returns `Some(AuraConsensusId)` if found in metadata, `None` otherwise
       - Early returns `None` if Aura pallet missing from metadata

    2. **Updated `DefaultRuntimeResolver::runtime()`**:
       - Calls `metadata_inspector.aura_consensus_id()` first
       - Uses detected type immediately (no warning needed)
       - Falls back to `aura_id_from_chain_spec_id()` only when detection returns `None`

    3. **Added test coverage**:
       - `test_aura_consensus_id()` verifies metadata detection finds authority ID type patterns correctly

    ## Behavior

    - If metadata contains Aura authority ID type → uses detected type (best accuracy)
    - If metadata unavailable or detection fails → falls back to chain spec ID check with warnings (from #11026)

crates:
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch